                %li
                  %a{:href => "#SwamplandCobordismConjectureReferences"} Swampland cobordism conjecture
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Several classes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacua"} string theory vacua
            require the presence of exactly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/24"} 24
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            4 transverse to a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                on an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptically+fibered+K3-surface"} elliptically fibered K3-surface
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
                (
                %a{:href => "#Sen96"}> Sen 96, p. 5
                ),
            %li
              %p
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HET-theory"} HET-theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
                with vanishing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton+number"} instanton number
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
                (
                %a{:href => "#Schwarz96"}> Schwarz 96, p. 50
                ).
          %p
            In both cases the condition arises as a kind of
            = succeed "-condition," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpole+cancellation"} tadpole cancellation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            = succeed "-fiber" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
          %p Despite the superficial similarity, this subtle effect is, at the face of it, rather different in the two cases:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                it results from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kodeira+classification"} Kodeira classification
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibrations"} elliptic fibrations
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptically+fibered+K3"} elliptically fibered K3
                has exactly 24 singular points, counted with multiplicity,
            %li
              %p
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HET-theory"} HET-theory
                it results, via the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
                being 24, and hence vanishing, via the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare-Hopf+theorem"} Poincare-Hopf theorem
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
                loci are cut out.
          %p
            An argument that these two different-looking mechanisms are in fact equivalent, under suitable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BraunBrodieLukasRuehle18"} Braun-Brodie-Lukas-Ruehle 18, Sec. III
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AspinwallMorrison97"} Aspinwall-Morrison 97
          %h3#InFTheoryOnK3 In F-theory on K3
          %p
            In passing from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            in 11d becomes the locus of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            in 10d. The locus of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            in turn (as discussed there) is the locus where the
            = succeed "-circle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A \times S^1_B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            degenerates to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-dual
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            in F-theory “are” the singular locus of the elliptic fibration.
          %p
            Now, considering
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory+on+K3"} F-theory on K3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptically+fibered+complex+K3-surface"} elliptically fibered complex K3-surface
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                          %mn 3
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℂ
                          %msup
                            %mi ℙ
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; K3
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{C}\mathbb{P}^1
                  }
          %p
            may be parameterized via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weierstrass+elliptic+function"} Weierstrass elliptic function
            as the solution locus of the equation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  y^2 = x^3 + f(z) x + g(z)
          %p
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z \in \mathbb{C}\mathbb{P}^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            of degree 8 and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            of degree twelve. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            of the complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            which this parameterizes for given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 24
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 3
                    %mrow
                      %mn 27
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mn 4
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j(\tau(z)) = \frac{4 (24 f)^3}{27 g^2 + 4 f^3}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poles"} poles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\to \infty
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            correspond to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            are located.
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:alt => "homotopy pasting diagram exhibiting the homotopy Whitehead integral", :src => "/nlab/files/K3CobordismBetween24ThreeSpheres.jpg", :width => "260px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Cohomotopy+and+Oriented+Cohomology+Theory"} SS21
          %p
            Since the order of the poles is 24 (the polynomial degree of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discriminant"} discriminant
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 27
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mn 4
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta = 27 g^2 + 4 f^3
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptically+fibered+K3-surface"} elliptically fibered K3-surface
                –
                %a{:href => "elliptic+fibration+of+a+K3-surface#SingularPoints"} singular points
            %em 24 D7-branes
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sen96"}> Sen 96, page 5
            ,
            %a{:href => "#Lerche99"} Lerche 99, p. 6
            , see also
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Morrison04"} Morrison 04, sections 8 and 17
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Denef08"} Denef 08, around (3.41)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "duality+between+M%2FF-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory#DouglasParkSchnell14"} Douglas-Park-Schnell 14
          %p
            Notice that the
            %em net charge
            of these 24 D7-branes is supposed to vanish, due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            effects (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Denef08"} Denef 08, below (3.41)
          %h3#in_iiatheory_on_k3 In IIA-theory on K3
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            the
            %a{:href => "#InFTheoryOnK3"} above
            discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            translates to 24
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            (
            %a{:href => "#Vafa96"}> Vafa 96, Footnote 2 on p. 6
            ).
          %h3#in_hettheory_on_k3 In HET-theory on K3
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            with vanishing
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton+number"} instanton number
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
            is implied by the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            measuring the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
            charge satisfies
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} trac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d H_3 = \trac{1}{2} p_1(\nabla)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mn 3
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi K
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mn 24
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{K3} \tfrac{1}{2} p_1(\nabla)  = \int_{K3} \chi_4(\nabla) = \chi_4[K3] = 24
            this implies, with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stokes%27+theorem"} Stokes' theorem
            = succeed "-flux" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-spheres"} 3-spheres
            around transversal
            = succeed "-punctures" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "duality+in+string+theory#Schwarz97"} Schwarz 96, around p. 50
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AspinwallMorrison97"} Aspinwall-Morrison 97, Sec. 4-5
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Johnson98"} Johnson 98, p. 30
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BraunBrodieLukasRuehle18"} Braun-Brodie-Lukas-Ruehle 18, Section III.A
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ChoiKobayashi19"} Choi-Kobayashi 19, Sec. 1.1
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality
            of this HET-phenomenon with that in F-theory
            %a{:href => "#InFTheoryOnK3"} above
            is discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BraunBrodieLukasRuehle18"} Braun-Brodie-Lukas-Ruehle 18, Section III
          %h3#under_hypothesis_h Under Hypothesis H
          %p
            The vanishing of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
            of K3 after cutting out the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            of 24 points is precisely the mechanism which witnesses the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+of+a+group"} order
            24 of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/third+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} third stable homotopy group of spheres
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin%27s+theorem"} Pontryagin's theorem
            as the existence of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+manifold"} framed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mn 3
                  %mo ∖
                  %mn 24
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K3 \setminus 24 \cdot D^4
            between 24
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-spheres"} 3-spheres
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/schreiber/files/24BranesTransversalToK3ViaHypothesisH-20210207.jpg", :width => "700px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/M-Theory+as+Mf-Theory"} SS21
          %p
            This relates the number of 24 branes transverse on K3 to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/schreiber/files/KKOn24PuncturedK3ViaHypothesisH-20210207.jpg", :width => "760px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/M-Theory+as+Mf-Theory"} SS21
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M%2FF-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between M/F-theory and heterotic string theory
          %h2#references References
          %h3#in_ftheory In F-theory
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kodeira+classification"} Kodeira classification
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptically+fibered+K3s"} elliptically fibered K3s
          %ul
            %li#Sen96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em F-theory and Orientifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9605150"} arXiv:hep-th/9605150
            %li#Lerche99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Lerche"}> Wolfgang Lerche
                ,
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9910207.pdf#page=6"} p. 6
                of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Heterotic/F-Theory Duality in Eight Dimensions
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Progress in String Theory and M-Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9910207"} arXiv:hep-th/9910207
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-010-0852-5_2"} doi:10.1007/978-94-010-0852-5_2
            %li#Morrison04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Morrison"}> David Morrison
                ,
                %em TASI Lectures on Compactification and Duality
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0411120"}> arXiv:hep-th/0411120
                )
            %li#Denef08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frederik+Denef"}> Frederik Denef
                ,
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0803.1194.pdf#page=34"} p. 34
                of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Les Houches Lectures on Constructing String Vacua
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+theory+and+the+real+world"} String theory and the real world
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0803.1194"}> arXiv:0803.1194
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/780946"} spire:780946
            %li#DouglasParkSchnell14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Douglas"}> Michael Douglas
                , Daniel S. Park, Christian Schnell,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Cremmer-Scherk Mechanism in F-theory Compactifications on K3 Manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1403.1595"} arXiv:1403.1595
          %h3#in_hettheory In HET-theory
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            on K3 (see also at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+instantons"} small instantons
          %ul
            %li#Schwarz96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"}> John Schwarz
                , around
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9607201.pdf#page=51"} p. 50
                of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Superstring and M Theory Dualities
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9607201"} arXiv:hep-th/9607201
            %li#Johnson98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Johnson"}> Clifford Johnson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Études on D-Branes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
                et. al. (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nonperturbative aspects of strings, branes and supersymmetry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9812196"} arXiv:hep-th/9812196
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/481393"} spire:481393
            %li#ChoiKobayashi19
              %p
                Kang-Sin Choi, Tatsuo Kobayashi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Transitions of Orbifold Vacua
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11194"} arXiv:1901.11194
          %h3#in_f_and_hettheory In F- and HET-theory
          %p
            Joint discussion in F- and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} dual
            HET-theory:
          %ul
            %li#AspinwallMorrison97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Aspinwall"}> Paul Aspinwall
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Morrison"} David Morrison
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Point-like Instantons on K3 Orbifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9705104"} arXiv:hep-th/9705104
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00516-6"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00516-6
            %li#BraunBrodieLukasRuehle18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Braun"}> Andreas Braun
                , Callum Brodie,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabian+Ruehle"} Fabian Ruehle
                = succeed "," do
                  %em NS5-Branes and Line Bundles in Heterotic/F-Theory Duality
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.06190"} arXiv:1803.06190
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.98.126004"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.98.126004
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in the context of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+line+bundles"} heterotic line bundles
          %div
            %h3#SwamplandCobordismConjectureReferences Swampland cobordism conjecture
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a{:href => "swampland#SwamplandCobordismConjecture"} swampland cobordism conjecture
              is the hypothesis that consistency of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacuum"} vacua
              in
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
              (hence their being in the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"}> landscape
              ” instead of the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/swampland"}> swampland
              ”) requires (undefined)
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} stringy
              = succeed "-analogs" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+groups"} cobordism groups
              to vanish:
            %ul
              %li#McNamaVafa17
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+McNamara"}> Jacob McNamara
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                  %em Cobordism Classes and the Swampland
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.10355"}> arXiv:1909.10355
                  ,
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1755441"} spire:1755441
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miguel+Montero"}> Miguel Montero
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Cobordism Conjecture, Anomalies, and the String Lamppost Principle
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.11729"} arXiv:2008.11729
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Dierigl"}> Markus Dierigl
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"} Jonathan Heckman
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On the Swampland Cobordism Conjecture and Non-Abelian Duality Groups
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.00013"} arXiv:2012.00013
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"}> Hirosi Ooguri
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadashi+Takayanagi"} Tadashi Takayanagi
                  %em Cobordism Conjecture in AdS
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.13953"}> arXiv:2006.13953
                  )
            %p
              A more concrete consequence of this conjecture is claimed (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.10355.pdf#page=31"}> McNamara-Vafa 17, Sec. 5.2, 2nd paragr.
              ) to be the statement that – paraphrasing/extrapolating somewhat:
              = succeed ";" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} brane charges are quantized
                  in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cobordism+cohomology"} Cobordism cohomology
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpole+cancellation"} tadpole cancellation
                of brane charges is to happen in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cobordism+cohomology"} Cobordism cohomology
              This statement is discussed, as a consequence of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.01877.pdf#page=83"} p. 83
            %ul
              %li#SatiSchreiber21a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/M-Theory+as+Mf-Theory"} M/F-Theory as Mf-Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.01877"}> arXiv:2103.01877
                )
